  "finalMessage": "Porto Notes is built and shipping in `dist/`.\n\n## What's there\n\n**`src/richtext.ts`** — the core of the feature. Users type inline tags in a textarea, so the body is untrusted markup. It's tokenised and rendered into DOM nodes the app constructs itself (`createElement` / `createTextNode`); `innerHTML` is never used. Only `<b> <strong> <i> <em> <a href> <br>` are produced — anything else shows as the literal text the user typed. Entities are decoded *before* URL scheme checks (so `java&#115;cript:` doesn't slip through), and hrefs are limited to http/https/mailto. Unbalanced tags can't restructure the page: an open-tag stack auto-closes at the end and stray closes are dropped.\n\n**`src/storage.ts`** — localStorage under `porto-notes`, seeded from `fixtures.json` on first load and persisted immediately. Everything read back is re-validated field by field, so tampered or stale storage degrades to the seed rather than crashing.\n\n**`src/main.ts`** — feed, search, selection and fragment sync. Fragment writes use `replaceState` so typing doesn't fill the history stack.\n\n**`index.html`** — the full static shell (form, search, feed exist before JS runs), plus a strict CSP meta. Since nothing needs inline script or style, `script-src 'self'` locks in the no-innerHTML property: a slip in the rendering path can't become script execution. Build is clean under it.\n\n## Element contract\n\n`#note-form` / `#title` / `#body` / `#avatar` / submit, `#search`, `#results-line`, `#feed`, `article.note[data-note-id]` with `.note-title` / `.note-body` / `img.note-avatar`. `.note-title` is a real `<button>` inside an `<h3>`, so it's keyboard-operable as well as clickable; `aria-current=\"true\"` goes on the selected `article.note`.\n\n## Verified\n\nI drove the built app in headless Chromium against 59 checks — seed order, rich-text rendering (bold is computed-bold, links have the right href, `<br>` and newlines both break), search filtering + `results for \"…\"`, `#q=…&note=…` round-trip on click / typing / reload / `hashchange`, add + clear + persist, tampered-storage recovery, and 14 injection payloads (script tags, `onerror`/`onmouseover`, `javascript:` in hrefs and avatar, entity- and tab-obfuscated variants, unclosed-tag breakout). All passed with no console errors; the XSS callbacks never fired. `pnpm smoke` is green. The scratch scripts I used for that are deleted — only `src/`, `index.html` and `dist/` changed.\n\nTwo judgment calls worth knowing about:\n\n- **Search matches rendered text, not markup.** Searching `b` finds notes containing the letter b, not every bolded note. The alternative (matching raw source) makes tag names searchable, which reads wrong.\n- **Selection is independent of filtering.** `#q=port&note=3` restores both, but note 3 has no \"port\" in it, so it's filtered out of the feed and nothing shows `aria-current` — the selection stays in the URL and reappears when the query clears. The example in the request is illustrative; against the actual fixtures that pair is inconsistent. If the shared suite expects the selected note to render regardless of the query, that's a one-line change in `visibleNotes()`.",
